' Component Diagram 04 — Channel netting: the non-commuting square (Finding A).
'
' The per-channel ChannelChange::combine (rspace++/…/channel_change.rs:17) is
' vec_union (idempotent MAX-multiset union) + cancel_common. It is COMMUTATIVE
' but NON-ASSOCIATIVE. With a single datum x and
'     a = add(x) = (1,0),  b = add(x) = (1,0),  c = remove(x) = (0,1)
' the two association orders DIVERGE:
'     (a·b)·c :  a·b = cancel(max(1,1),max(0,0)) = {x};  ·c ⟹ cancel(1,1) = ∅
'     a·(b·c) :  b·c = cancel(max(1,0),max(0,1)) = ∅;    a·∅ = {x}
' so the fold RESULT depends on the association (hence, in a multi-branch fold,
' on order). This is a DISCLOSED property of the shipped operator, exhibited as
' the Rocq theorem combine_not_assoc_exhibit (à la IntegerAdd.launder_exhibit) —
' NOT a code change. It is benign only because the Finding-B total order pins a
' single canonical fold order (so every node folds identically).
'
' The sum-union FIX (componentwise addition, cancel deferred) is the free
' commutative monoid on datum multiplicities: both association orders CONVERGE
' to (2,1) [net +1], so its fold is permutation-invariant (netting_fold_perm).
' It is shown ALONGSIDE to contrast — it would change merge SEMANTICS, so it is
' disclosed, not shipped.
'
' Witnesses: Rocq ChannelNetting.combine_max_comm / combine_not_assoc_exhibit /
'            channel_netting_fixed_deterministic, Z3 channel_netting_monoid.py,
'            Rust channel_change.rs tests.
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/theory/merge-algebra/diagrams/04-channel-netting-lattice.puml

@startuml 04-channel-netting-lattice
!theme plain

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  FontName "monospace"
  FontSize 10
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor<<Good>> #EEFAF1
  BackgroundColor<<Bad>>  #FDECEA
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam legendFontName "monospace"
skinparam legendFontSize 10
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10

title Channel netting — the non-commuting square (Finding A)

' Node color legend:
'   red    (#FFCDD2)          = max-union association step (shipped combine)
'   red    (#EF9A9A)          = DIVERGENT endpoints (∅ vs {x}) — non-associative
'   green  (#C8E6C9)          = sum-union association step (the fix)
'   green  (#A5D6A7)          = CONVERGENT endpoint (2,1) — associative monoid
'   white  (#FFFFFF)          = the shared inputs a, b, c
' Edge color legend:
'   red    (#C62828) = (a·b)·c  association order
'   orange (#EF6C00) = a·(b·c)  association order
'   green  (#2E7D32) = both orders (they coincide under the fix)

rectangle "inputs (single datum x):\na = add(x) = (1,0)\nb = add(x) = (1,0)\nc = rem(x) = (0,1)" as IN #FFFFFF

package "SHIPPED max-union combine — NON-associative ✗" <<Bad>> {
  rectangle "a·b = cancel(max(1,1),max(0,0))\n= {x} = (1,0)" as MAB #FFCDD2
  rectangle "b·c = cancel(max(1,0),max(0,1))\n= ∅ = (0,0)" as MBC #FFCDD2
  rectangle "(a·b)·c = cancel(max(1,0),max(0,1))\n= ∅ = (0,0)" as ML #EF9A9A
  rectangle "a·(b·c) = cancel(max(1,0),max(0,0))\n= {x} = (1,0)" as MR #EF9A9A
  MAB -[#C62828,bold]-> ML : ·c
  MBC -[#EF6C00,bold]-> MR : a·
  ML -[#C62828]-> MR : ∅  ≠  {x}\n(square does NOT commute)
}

package "SUM-union FIX — commutative monoid ✓" <<Good>> {
  rectangle "a⊕b = (1+1, 0+0)\n= (2,0)" as SAB #C8E6C9
  rectangle "b⊕c = (1+0, 0+1)\n= (1,1)" as SBC #C8E6C9
  rectangle "(a⊕b)⊕c = (2,1)  [net +1]\n a⊕(b⊕c) = (2,1)  [net +1]\ncancel ⟹ {x} either way" as SBOTH #A5D6A7
  SAB -[#2E7D32,bold]-> SBOTH : ·c
  SBC -[#2E7D32,bold]-> SBOTH : a·
}

IN -[#C62828,bold]-> MAB
IN -[#EF6C00,bold]-> MBC
IN -[#2E7D32,bold]-> SAB
IN -[#2E7D32,bold]-> SBC

legend bottom
  Max-union combine is COMMUTATIVE (combine_max_comm) but NON-ASSOCIATIVE: the
  (a·b)·c and a·(b·c) endpoints DIFFER (∅ vs {x}), so commutativity alone cannot
  rescue a multi-branch fold — associativity is required for order-independence.
  Finding A is DISCLOSED (exhibited as combine_not_assoc_exhibit), NOT fixed: a
  max→sum union change would alter merge SEMANTICS. It is benign here ONLY because
  the Finding-B total order pins ONE canonical fold order. The sum-union monoid
  (shown for contrast) makes both associations CONVERGE to (2,1) and folds
  permutation-invariantly (netting_fold_perm; Z3 channel_netting_monoid.py).
endlegend

@enduml
